# Dijkstra's Algorithm with a Binary Min-Heap

## The Core Idea

Dijkstra finds the shortest path from a source node to all other nodes. It works by repeatedly selecting the **unvisited node with the smallest known distance**, then relaxing its edges. The binary heap makes the "smallest distance" selection efficient.

## Binary Min-Heap Priority Queue

The heap lets us extract the minimum-distance node in **O(log n)** instead of scanning all nodes in **O(n)**.

